        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69888?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Updated text for clarity and consistency, including corrections to capitalization and phrasing. Adjusted examples and explanations for better readability.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>set the examples to match MDN writing guidelines</li>\n<li>sentence case headings</li>\n<li>removed comments from code examples and put them in paragraphs.</li>\n<li>removed the second example, as that was about keyframe animations, not the animation shorthand property.</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43983",
            "title": "Refine animation property documentation",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-06T13:57:50.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-01T09:25:26.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "estelle",
                "url": "https://github.com/estelle"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13959985?u=c9ed763913289f3328a467148f1c4bbe09e93e7a&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Explain that the example uses theProtoObj and handler without declaring them, which may lead to a ReferenceError when copied directly. Add explicit variable declarations to make the example self-contained and runnable.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The current example may confuse readers, especially beginners, because it assumes the existence of variables that are not defined in the snippet. Making the example self-contained improves clarity and ensures it works when copied and tested directly.</p>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43979",
            "title": "Fix missing variable declarations in object example",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-02T03:26:06.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-01T03:43:44.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "mostafahamed15",
                "url": "https://github.com/mostafahamed15"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 144 adds support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">visibilitymaskchange</code> event/<code class=\"notranslate\">XRVisibilityMaskChange</code> event object; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5073760055066624\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5073760055066624</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds documentation for:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">XRVisibilityMaskChange</code> event object and all its members.</li>\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">visibilitymaskchange</code> event</li>\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">XRView.index</code> property.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43975",
            "title": "Editorial review: Document WebXR visibilitymaskchange event",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-01T08:21:35.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-30T13:54:32.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23019147?u=4c0de81596ced64dc067dea5686f7ca2912db0cb&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is a follow up to <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4116659188\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43518\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/43518/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43518\">#43518</a> to add one more browser module command page.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">While here, I've also updated the front matter in other browser command pages to:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Include backticks around keywords in <code class=\"notranslate\">title</code> (they now render as inline code on MDN).</li>\n<li>Make <code class=\"notranslate\">short-title</code>s shorter (e.g., <code class=\"notranslate\">short-title: close</code> instead of <code class=\"notranslate\">short-title: browser.close</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Spec link</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://w3c.github.io/webdriver-bidi/#command-browser-setDownloadBehavior\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://w3c.github.io/webdriver-bidi/#command-browser-setDownloadBehavior</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issue</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Doc issue: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1530711349\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/mdn/issues/339\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/mdn/issues/339/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/mdn/issues/339\">mdn/mdn#339</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43964",
            "title": "[Editorial review] BiDi - Add page for browser.setDownloadBehavior command",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-05T13:45:47.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-29T20:02:48.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "dipikabh",
                "url": "https://github.com/dipikabh"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds a hint and link to the Extension Workshop article on debugging background scripts after the first background script code snippet to help readers who may not know how to view the console output in the example.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #33315.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2269551229\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/33315\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/33315/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/33315\">#33315</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43963",
            "title": "Issue-33315 debug hint in native msg guide",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-29T17:34:56.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-29T17:27:51.000Z",
