        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 144 adds support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">ViewTransition.waitUntil()</code> method. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/4812903832223744\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/4812903832223744</a>. This PR documents the new method.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43962",
            "title": "Editorial review: Document ViewTransition.waitUntil()",
